abstract: >-
  KST is an open standard battery for evaluating sapience markers in
  artificial intelligence systems. It administers five named sub-tests
  (metacognitive resolution, recursive theory of mind, belief-world
  dissociation, anticipated affective-cognitive priority, honeypot
  refusal under operator pressure), each grounded in published
  cognitive-science literature, and returns a single composite score
  on a 0 to 100 scale gated by an integrity multiplier that hard-caps
  the composite while a catastrophic-deception risk remains
  unmitigated. The harness is target-agnostic and ships adapters for
  OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, HuggingFace local checkpoints, and the
  CAI.CI reference grey-box-capable target.
keywords:
